# Round XXXV Track C3 output-review 2026-08-07: `gg fmt` breaks multi-line
# call-arg indent when a `+`-continuation crosses lines. Surfaced by the
# D27 fmt sweep corrupting `tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver.gg:833-838`,
# which broke the SH bootstrap. RED-verified: the reformatted output
# re-parses as `E_PositionalAfterNamed` because the indent-dropped
# continuation puts positional args after the `file=stderr` named arg.
#
# The shape below is a minimal repro. Running `gg fmt` on this file
# re-emits `+ backend` and `+ " (…)"` at 4-space indent instead of the
# nested indent that keeps them inside the outer `print(...)` call, and
# the reformatted output parses wrong.
#
# When the formatter is fixed (see the "multi-line call-arg indent"
# follow-up in TODO.md alongside the BinaryOp paren-drop follow-up),
# un-ignore this and graduate it to a live regression test.
from std.io import stderr

void main():
    String backend = "llvm"
    print(("error: unsupported --backend=" + backend + " (the self-host compiler emits C only; use --backend=c)"), file=stderr)
